# Verifies: SPEC §3.1 (floating-point literals) / D-LEX-04 float literals / D-DIAG-02 E0004
# At least one digit is required on both sides of the decimal point; both `.5` and `5.`
# are lexical errors. Lexing stops at the first invalid literal it encounters, so this
# file targets the digit missing right after the decimal point (`5.`).

x = 5.
